{"name":"Crispy Gingersnap","hex":"#bb7838","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crispy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a crisp texture; brittle yet tender.","Denoting something is impressive or desirable; cool, awesome; fresh."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The well-baked fat on the surface of a piece of roasted meat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crispy"},{"term":"gingersnap","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of biscuit or cookie made from dough seasoned with ginger.","A hot-tempered person, particularly one who is red-haired."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gingersnap"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crispiness","blocks":[{"text":"Crispiness or crispness is one of the most common food texture attributes. Crispiness refers to a hard food that emits a sound upon fracturing. Foods described as crisp tend not to show signs of deformation prior to fracture. Crispiness and crunchiness are often used interchangeably, however crispiness tends to be associated with a higher pitched sound, while crunchiness is associated with lower pitched sounds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Pernil.1.jpg/330px-Pernil.1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crispiness","wikidata":"Q5186058"},{"title":"Ginger snap","blocks":[{"text":"A gingersnap, ginger snap, ginger nut, or ginger biscuit is a biscuit flavoured with ginger. Ginger snaps are flavoured with powdered ginger and a variety of other spices, most commonly cinnamon, molasses and clove. There are many recipes. The brittle ginger nut style is a commercial version of the traditional fairings once made for market fairs now represented only by the Cornish fairing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Arnott%27s_Ginger_Nut_04.jpg/330px-Arnott%27s_Ginger_Nut_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c